    "problem_statement": "# JSON output in PrettyTable is broken when using fields option\n\n## Description\n\nWhen using the `get_json_string()` method with the `fields` option, the JSON output is incorrect. The header and field filtering logic appears to be reversed.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n```python\nfrom prettytable import PrettyTable\n\n# Create a simple table\nt = PrettyTable()\nt.field_names = [\"Field 1\", \"Field 2\", \"Field 3\"]\nt.add_row([1, \"value 1\", \"value2\", \"value3\"])\nt.add_row([4, \"value 4\", \"value5\", \"value6\"])\nt.add_row([7, \"value 7\", \"value8\", \"value9\"])\n\n# Try to get JSON with specific fields\noptions = {'fields': ['Field 1', 'Field 3']}\nresult = t.get_json_string(**options)\nprint(result)\n```\n\n### Expected output\nThe JSON should contain only the specified fields:\n```\n[\n    [\n        \"Field 1\",\n        \"Field 3\"\n    ],\n    {\n        \"Field 1\": \"value 1\",\n        \"Field 3\": \"value3\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"Field 1\": \"value 4\",\n        \"Field 3\": \"value6\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"Field 1\": \"value 7\",\n        \"Field 3\": \"value9\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\n### Actual output\nThe JSON contains all fields instead of just the specified ones, or the header is incorrect:\n```\n[\n    [\n        \"Field 1\",\n        \"Field 2\",\n        \"Field 3\"\n    ],\n    {\n        \"Field 1\": \"value 1\",\n        \"Field 3\": \"value3\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"Field 1\": \"value 4\",\n        \"Field 3\": \"value6\"\n    },\n    {\n        \"Field 1\": \"value 7\",\n        \"Field 3\": \"value9\"\n    }\n]\n```\n\nThe issue appears to be in the logic that handles the header and fields filtering in the `get_json_string()` method."
  },
